#: ../../../index.rst:3
msgid "pipx"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../index.rst:5
msgid ""
"``pipx`` installs and runs end-user Python applications in isolated "
"environments. It fills the same role as macOS's `brew <https://brew.sh>`_, "
"JavaScript's `npx <https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/commands/npx>`_, and Linux's "
"`apt <https://wiki.debian.org/Apt>`_. Under the hood it uses `uv <https://"
"docs.astral.sh/uv/>`_ when available and `pip <https://pip.pypa.io>`_ "
"otherwise, but unlike either it creates a separate virtual environment for "
"each application, so their dependencies never collide and an uninstall "
"leaves nothing behind."
msgstr ""

